USE smart_cafeteria;

-- ===========================================================================
-- Seed data for local development and the demo.
-- ===========================================================================
-- Two parts:
--   1. Reference data (counters, menu, demo accounts) — what you need to log in.
--   2. Fourteen days of synthetic operational history — what you need for the
--      admin dashboard, the reporting views and the DES calibration to have
--      anything to say on a fresh install.
--
-- Part 2 is generated, not measured, and the data says so: every service_events
-- row carries source='simulated', so nobody can mistake it for real cafeteria
-- readings in a viva.  Delete from the "PART 2" banner downwards for a clean
-- database, or set DES_USE_DB_CALIBRATION=false to have the DES engine ignore it.
--
-- Statements are batched in groups of 100 rows so phpMyAdmin's import does not
-- time out on a single enormous INSERT.
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- PART 1 — reference data
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

